# Build-context controls for docker/worker.Dockerfile (architecture plan
# Section 22) -- this is the DEFAULT build context for `docker build` with
# no -f, and for `-f docker/worker.Dockerfile` specifically. The Dockerfile
# only ever COPYs requirements/worker.lock and src/ explicitly, but this
# file is still the single source of truth for what may enter the build
# context at all -- defence in depth against a future Dockerfile edit, and
# it keeps the context small regardless. These worker protections are
# unchanged by the rule below.
#
# A Dockerfile with different context needs gets its own
# "<Dockerfile>.dockerignore" instead of loosening this file -- Docker
# picks that sibling file up automatically for a matching `-f` build.
# docker/probe.Dockerfile uses docker/probe.Dockerfile.dockerignore (a
# minimal allowlist: exclude everything, re-include only what that
# Dockerfile's own COPY steps need), since it needs scripts/
# connectivity_probe.py, which this file deliberately excludes below.

# Git metadata and local environments
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.cache

# The Streamlit lab -- never part of the worker image
app.py
src/xtra_takehome/app/

# Not needed at runtime
tests/
docs/
scripts/
docker/
infra/
reports/
run.sh
run.ps1
README.md
AGENTS.md
AIUSAGE.md
AWS_DESIGN.md
pyproject.toml

# Dev/control-plane locks -- the worker image installs only worker.lock
requirements/dev.in
requirements/dev.lock
requirements/control.in
requirements/control.lock

# Editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
